The A10/A20 TV encoders can drive a VGA connector: in "VGA mode" three
DACs output R, G and B straight from the display backend, and TCON
channel 1 drives HSYNC/VSYNC. The Cubietruck wires its VGA connector
this way and the vendor 3.4 kernel uses it as the default output, but
mainline has no VGA support for it.

Patch 1 lets the TCON drive a DAC (VGA) encoder on channel 1 and adds
the missing TV encoder case to the A10/A20 output mux. Patch 2 adds a
VGA mode to sun4i_tv when its output port links to a vga-connector, with
EDID and detection over the connector's DDC bus. Patch 3 adds the A20 TV
encoder nodes and the Cubietruck VGA output.

The register values come from the vendor driver and were checked against
a Cubietruck running it. Tested on a Cubietruck (A20, 2 GiB) with
Armbian's 6.18.56 and a 1280x1024 monitor: VGA alone, EDID and hot-plug,
DPMS, and VGA on TCON0 next to HDMI on TCON1. On v7.3-rc7 the series
builds with W=1; patch 2 needed a small rebase there (drm_encoder_init()
instead of drm_simple_encoder_init()) that was not run on hardware.

This is an RFC because of open design questions:

- Binding: allwinner,sun4i-a10-tv-encoder.yaml allows a single input
  "port" and requires "resets". Patch 3 uses "ports" (input and output)
  and no resets, so dtbs_check fails. A binding patch would add an
  output port; is that the way to go, or a separate A20 compatible?
- Reset: VGA works with the TV encoder's reset bit untouched (as the
  vendor driver leaves it), so patch 2 makes the reset optional for VGA.
  The A20 CCU does have RST_TVE0/1; VGA with that reset described and
  deasserted has not been tested yet.
- Connector: the VGA connector lives inside sun4i_tv. Would you rather
  see the generic display-connector bridge (vga-connector with
  ddc-i2c-bus) attached to the encoder?
- The output mux is keyed on the TCON id (TV encoder n is fed by TCON n
  only), which is how the device tree wires it.
- Known issue: an earlier version looked up the DDC adapter in the
  component bind and returned -EPROBE_DEFER there; the half-bound
  pipeline was torn down and the boot hung. This version no longer
  defers in bind for the DDC bus (the existing possible_crtcs check in
  bind still can), and why the teardown after a bind-time deferral hung
  was not analysed.

Two related fixes found during this work are posted separately: the
frontend routing of the second display pipeline, needed for video planes
on the second CRTC, and the backend hardware cursor.

Patch 3 is based on Chen-Yu Tsai's 2019 device tree work for the same
board (sun4i-drm-tve-vga-wip, linked in the patch). Chen-Yu, would you
prefer a Co-developed-by: there?

Investigation and patches were done with an AI assistant; I reviewed the
result and tested it on the hardware named above.

